course: dictionary
lesson: 14548
title: Asking words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some prayers say thank you, some say sorry, some praise God, and some ask for something. A prayer that asks is called petitionary. So petitionary means asking for something, and a petitionary prayer asks God for help or for something needed.
explain: Use the clues in the sentence to work out a new word. «Mum said a petitionary prayer for Grandad, asking God to help him feel better.» The words asking God to help are the clues. A petitionary prayer is a prayer that asks for something.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The class wrote petitionary prayers for families who had no food.» If you put asking for help in place of petitionary, the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
fact: Petitionary means asking for something.
fact: A petitionary prayer asks God for help or for something that is needed.
fact: A petitionary prayer can be for yourself or for other people.
fact: Other kinds of prayer are praise, thanks and saying sorry.
fact: Petitionary is a formal word, mostly used in church and religion lessons.
exercise: «Mia said a petitionary prayer before the test, asking God to help her stay calm.» What does petitionary mean? | Saying thank you for something | *Asking for something | Saying sorry for something | Singing a happy song
exercise: «The petitionary prayer on the card asked God to keep the family safe.» What kind of prayer is this? | Praise, for how great God is | *A prayer that asks for help | Thanks for a good day | Saying sorry for a wrong thing
exercise: Find and copy the word in «Our class said a petitionary prayer for the sick children, asking God to help them.» that tells you the prayer asks for something. | *asking | sick | class | children
test: «Ben said a petitionary prayer for his cousin, who was ill.» What kind of prayer was it? | Thanking God for a birthday party | Praising God for a sunny sky | *A prayer that asks for help for someone else | Saying sorry for a broken promise
test: Which of these is a petitionary prayer? | Saying sorry for breaking a window | Thanking God for a birthday party | *Asking God to help the people who have no homes | Praising God for the beautiful sunrise
exam: Which best describes a petitionary prayer? | *A prayer that asks for something needed | A prayer that sings praise | A prayer that gives thanks | A prayer that says sorry
